<title>FINLAND: OKOBANK TO ISSUE 250 MLN MARKKA DEBENTURE.</title>
<headline>OKOBANK TO ISSUE 250 MLN MARKKA DEBENTURE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish banking group OKOBANK said on Thursday it would issue together with co-operative banks a 250 million markka six-year variable rate debenture with a 5.00 percent coupon.</p>
<p>The subscription period runs from March 18 to June 18, 1997 and the bond will be fully repaid on March 18, 2003, OKOBANK said in a statement.</p>
<p>A bourse listing will be sought for the bond after the subscription period, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 240, news@Reuters.fi</p>
